Each named document contains zero or more lines in `key=value` form. Empty keys and lines without `=` are malformed; values may be empty and may contain additional `=` characters. Document names must be nonempty and unique. Produce `cache_json` as a JSON object whose document keys are sorted lexicographically; each value is another JSON object with entry keys sorted lexicographically. Later duplicate keys within one document replace earlier values. Correctly JSON-escape quotes, backslashes, newlines, carriage returns, and tabs in names, keys, and values.

`id_document` contains one unsigned decimal `u64` per nonempty line. Whitespace surrounding an ID is ignored. Any other nonempty line is invalid. Return IDs in ascending order with duplicates removed. Empty inputs produce `{"cache":{}}` only if that were the requested format—but the actual required cache is the direct empty object string `{}` and an empty ID vector. Do not mutate either input. Provide a new complete implementation without `main`.

